# One line ending everywhere: LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the machines this is worked on, which stores LF and
# checks out CRLF. That is harmless in itself, but it means a file written by a
# tool (LF) and the same file after a checkout (CRLF) differ byte for byte —
# which breaks the md5 verification the harness deployment relies on, and makes
# every checkout look like it changed every file.
#
# LF is also what is served: the harness runs from an IIS web root, and the
# module runs inside REDCap on Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and not to be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
